<title>USA: Ascend to use Rockwell technology.</title>
<headline>Ascend to use Rockwell technology.</headline>
<dateline>ALAMEDA, Calif. 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ascend Communications Inc said Tuesday it will use Rockwell International Corp's 56 kilobytes per second, high speed modem technology in its line of MAX products.</p>
<p>Ascend, a maker of networking products that boost capabilities for existing computer networks, said Rockwell's modem technology will help increase the speed which internet service providers and carriers offer their customers.</p>
<p>Ascend said it expects to offer the Rockwell technology in its MAX products in 1997.</p>
</text>
